      "message": "I think this is a right annotation.\n\nI want to make sure BpfNetMaps call `native_addUidInterfaceRules` only when BpfNetMaps acquire lock of “sUidOwnerMap” which is done by `synchronized (sUidOwnerMap) {…}`.\nnative_addUidInterfaceRules internally hold mMutex lock but this lock is not shared with Java code.\nSo, while migration from JNI to Java codes, some BpfNetMaps API will acquire both lock of `sUidOwnerMap` in Java and `mMutex` in TrafficController.\nOtherwise, JNI could update the bpf map while java code is updating the bpf map.\nAfter migration, we can remove mMutex and BpfNetMaps will acquire lock of only `sUidOwnerMap` for sequential read and write.",
